-- title:
--   Comparison of the H=top and Igusa integral models
-- statement:
--   Let $N_0$ and $p$ be natural numbers with $p$ prime, $p \nmid N_0$, let $hpM$ witness $p \mid N_0p$, and let $hj$ witness that the $q$-series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the level-one $q$-expansion field $\mathbb Q$-field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` (the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms for $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$). Let $\mathfrak X$ be any inhabitant of `XHDRModelAtP p (N₀ * p) ⊤ hpM hj`, the two-chart integral model datum at level $N_0p$ with $H=\top$ over $R_p$, and let $\mathfrak P$ be any inhabitant of `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ p hpN₀`, the corresponding package built on the Igusa scheme `IgusaScheme (N₀ * p) p` with base map `IgusaScheme.igusaTo`; each of these data carries a curve model `Meta` of the relevant geometrically based function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, an isomorphism `eeta` onto the base change of the integral model along $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$, a Galois compatibility, a chart-reading pin, and sections $\varepsilon_\infty$, $\varepsilon_0$. The assertion is that there exist: an equality $hF$ of intermediate fields $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-generated inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$, namely `xHFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * p) ⊤ = modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * p)`; an isomorphism of schemes $\varphi$ from `XHDRLevel.X p (XHDRLevel.ΓM (N₀ * p) ⊤) hj` to `DRLevel.X N₀ p`; a proof that $\varphi$ followed by `DRLevel.toBase N₀ p` equals `XHDRLevel.toBase p (XHDRLevel.ΓM (N₀ * p) ⊤) hj`, so that $\varphi$ is an isomorphism over $\operatorname{Spec} R_p$; a proof that $\mathfrak X.\varepsilon_\infty$ followed by $\varphi$ equals $\mathfrak P.\varepsilon_\infty$; and, for these data, the statement that whenever $y$ is a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-point of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ over the base and $y_0$ is a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-point of $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ over the base such that $y$ followed by $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{eeta}$, the first pullback projection and $\varphi$ agrees with $y_0$ followed by $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{eeta}$ and the first projection of the pullback of `DRLevel.toBase N₀ p` along `genPt p`, then the place of $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{Meta}$ attached to $y_0$ by the bijection `pointEquivPlace` (points of the model over the algebraically closed base correspond to closed points, hence to places of the function field) is the transport, under `Place.congrRingEquiv` along the ring isomorphism given by $hF$, of the place of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{Meta}$ attached to $y$.
--
--   This is the comparison, at $H=\top$, between the two-chart Deligne–Rapoport-style integral model of $X_0(N_0p)$ over $\mathbb Z_{(p)}$ used in the $\Gamma_H$ family and the Igusa-scheme package for the same curve, in a form carrying compatibility with the base maps, the $\infty$-sections and the identification of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points with places of the geometric function field. It is the model-comparison input to the Néron-object arguments at $p$, and is cited in the analysis of the toric part and Frobenius–Hecke relations on $J_0(N_0p)$ through [`ModularCurve.toricFrobeniusHecke_toricMonodromyPart_jZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.toricFrobeniusHecke_toricMonodromyPart_jZero).
